{"name":"Anonymous","hex":"#dadcd3","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Anonymous","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A decentralized hacktivist group that conducts cyberattacks opposing primarily Internet censorship and government corruption.","A member of an anonymous imageboard website, especially of 4chan."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Anonymous"}],"entries":[{"title":"Anonymity","blocks":[{"text":"Anonymity describes situations in which the acting person's identity is unknown. Anonymity may be created unintentionally through the loss of identifying information due to the passage of time or a destructive event, or intentionally if a person chooses to withhold their identity."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Anonymous_Scientology_9_by_David_Shankbone.JPG/330px-Anonymous_Scientology_9_by_David_Shankbone.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anonymity"},{"title":"Anonymous work","blocks":[{"text":"Anonymous works are creative works, such as art or literature, that have an anonymous, undisclosed, or unknown creator or author. In the case of very old works, the author's name may simply be lost over the course of history and time. There are a number of reasons anonymous works arise. Examples include Beowulf and The Arabian Nights."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Stroop_Report_-_Warsaw_Ghetto_Uprising_09.jpg/330px-Stroop_Report_-_Warsaw_Ghetto_Uprising_09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anonymous_work"},{"title":"Anonymous (hacker group)","blocks":[{"text":"Anonymous is an international collective, organized as a decentralized group of activist and hacktivist individuals, best known for orchestrating cyberattacks against governments, government institutions, agencies, corporations, and the Church of Scientology."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Anonymous_emblem.svg/330px-Anonymous_emblem.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anonymous_(hacker_group)"},{"title":"Anonymous (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Anonymous is a 2011 period drama film directed by Roland Emmerich and written by John Orloff. The film is a fictionalized version of the life of Edward de Vere, 17th Earl of Oxford, an Elizabethan courtier, playwright, poet and patron of the arts, and suggests he was the actual author of William Shakespeare's plays. It stars Rhys Ifans as de Vere and Vanessa Redgrave as Queen Elizabeth I of England."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/5b/Anonymous_2011_film_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anonymous_(film)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Anonymous_Scientology_1_by_David_Shankbone.JPG/500px-Anonymous_Scientology_1_by_David_Shankbone.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Anonymous_Scientology_1_by_David_Shankbone.JPG/1280px-Anonymous_Scientology_1_by_David_Shankbone.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Anonymous_Scientology_1_by_David_Shankbone.JPG/500px-Anonymous_Scientology_1_by_David_Shankbone.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Protesters of the group Anonymous outside a Scientology center on February 10, 2008. Four of the protesters can be seen wearing Guy Fawkes masks","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAnonymous_Scientology_1_by_David_Shankbone.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Pasquino_02.jpg/